+
+## Bot moderation (flooding + failing webhooks + suspension)
+
+- Limits fixed in `User` constants (no settings): `BOT_RATE_LIMIT_COUNT=10`, `BOT_RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW=10s`, `BOT_COOLDOWN_DURATION=30s`, `BOT_COOLDOWN_SUSPEND_AFTER_ATTEMPTS=5` (1 initial +5 =6 total), `BOT_MAX_CONSECUTIVE_FAILURES=10`.
+- Columns `users`: `bot_suspended_at` datetime, `bot_suspension_reason` string (`rate_limit`|`webhook_failures`), `bot_cooldown_until` datetime, `bot_cooldown_attempts` int default 0, `bot_consecutive_failures` int default 0, `bot_rate_limit_reset_at` datetime (ignore pre-reactivate messages).
+  - Scopes `suspended`/`not_suspended` (`bot_suspended_at` nil check); suspended bots stay `status: active` so `bots_scope` (`User.bots.active`) still lists them and `bots_count` still includes them toward owner's limit.
+- Flooding (global per-bot, all rooms):
+  - Count via `messages.where(creator: bot).where(created_at > max(10s.ago, reset_at)).count` — sliding 10s window, counts both API posts and webhook sync replies (both create `Message`).
+  - `User#check_bot_post_allowed!` (with_lock): `:suspended` if suspended; if `in_bot_cooldown?` increment `bot_cooldown_attempts`, suspend on `>=6`, return `:in_cooldown`; clear expired cooldown; if count>=10 set `cooldown_until=30s.from_now`, `attempts=1`, return `:rate_limited`; else `:allowed`.
+  - `Rooms::BotMessagesController#create` order: 401 bad token → 403 suspended → 404 bad room/not member → 422 blank → 429 via `check_bot_post_allowed!` (`Retry-After: ceil(cooldown_until-now)` clamped 1..30) → 201. Empty/404 never start/increment cooldown. Suspend-triggering 5th-more still 429; next is 403.
+  - Sync replies (`BotWebhookNotifier#handle_ok_response`): membership re-check, then same `check_bot_post_allowed!`; `:allowed` posts, else suppressed (cooldown counts toward suspension). Blank/non-text/205+ handled before rate check (not counted).
+- Failing webhooks (both `mention` + `joined` via same `post_payload`/`handle_response`):
+  - Success = `2xx` (200/204/other 2xx all reset `bot_consecutive_failures=0` via `record_bot_delivery_success!`); only 200+text/plain|html|blank-CT with non-blank body posts sync reply, other 2xx ignored for reply but still success.
+  - Failure = non-2xx, timeout (`open 5s/read 10s`), connection error, invalid URL — `post_payload` rescue + `handle_response` else both call `record_bot_delivery_failure!` (with_lock increment, suspend on `>=10` with `webhook_failures`). Success resets.
+  - `record_*` no-op if already suspended; jobs never retry/crash (rescue+warn).
+- Suspended:
+  - `suspended?` = `bot? && bot_suspended_at.present?`; `suspension_reason_text`: `rate_limit`→`Flooding: too many messages`, `webhook_failures`→`Failing webhooks: too many consecutive failures`.
+  - Posting → 403 (checked before room/body so always 403); webhooks skipped at all layers: `BotMentionJob` query `not_suspended`, `BotJoinedJob` early return, `Room.memberships.grant_to` query `not_suspended`, `Membership#notify_bot_joined` check, `Notifier#notify/notify_joined` reload+`suspended?` early return + `handle_ok_response` re-check.
+  - Keeps rooms/messages (no delete), still counts (`User.bots.where(created_by:).count` includes suspended).
+  - `/bots` index: `<span>Suspended</span> — reason_text` for all viewers; admin-only `button_to "Reactivate"` (exact labels `Suspended`/`Reactivate`, `turbo_confirm` native confirm) → `POST /bots/:id/reactivate` (`BotsController#reactivate`, admin-only 403, non-suspended redirect, else `reactivate_bot!` clears suspend/reason/cooldown/attempts/failures + `reset_at=now` so immediate repost allowed).
+- Edge: cooldown global (any room 429); Retry-After ceil decreases; natural expiry clears on next post; webhook 200 during cooldown still success (resets failures) but reply suppressed+counts; 200-json/blank/204/201 success no message; 404/timeout/conn-refused failure; joined failures suspend same as mention; reactivate allows immediate post despite old 10 msgs (reset_at cutoff).
